KoboldCpp is one file. There is no installer. Pick your system, then click the file for your graphics card. Not sure which card you have? See [below](#which-graphics-card-do-i-have). Every link goes to the [latest official release on GitHub](https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest).

{% tabs syncKey="os" %}
{% tabitem label="Windows" %}

{% linkcard title="NVIDIA graphics card" description="koboldcpp.exe" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp.exe" /%}
{% linkcard title="AMD or Intel graphics, or none" description="koboldcpp-nocuda.exe, a much smaller download" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp-nocuda.exe" /%}
{% linkcard title="Older PC" description="koboldcpp-oldpc.exe, if the others crash at start" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp-oldpc.exe" /%}

{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Linux" %}

{% linkcard title="NVIDIA graphics card" description="koboldcpp-linux-x64" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp-linux-x64" /%}
{% linkcard title="AMD or Intel graphics, or none" description="koboldcpp-linux-x64-nocuda, a much smaller download" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp-linux-x64-nocuda" /%}
{% linkcard title="Older PC" description="koboldcpp-linux-x64-oldpc, if the others crash at start" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp-linux-x64-oldpc" /%}

{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="macOS" %}

{% linkcard title="Apple Silicon (M-series)" description="koboldcpp-mac-arm64" href="https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest/download/koboldcpp-mac-arm64" /%}

Intel Macs have no ready-made file. See [Build from source](/docs/install/from-source/#macos).

{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

{% aside type="caution" title="Only download from GitHub" %}
"You should **ONLY** trust official downloads from the release binaries on the official github at https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest". Quoted from the KoboldCpp README.
{% /aside %}

## Which graphics card do I have?

On Windows, the Task Manager shows it.

{% steps %}

1. Right-click an empty spot on the taskbar and click **Task Manager**. The keyboard shortcut is Ctrl+Shift+Esc.

   ![The menu after right-clicking the taskbar, with Task Manager highlighted](../../assets/docs/getting-started/windows-taskbar-menu.png)

2. Click **Performance**.

   ![Task Manager with Performance selected](../../assets/docs/getting-started/windows-task-manager-performance.png)

3. Click **GPU** in the list on the left. The card's name is at the top right. **Dedicated GPU memory** is the card's own memory, its **VRAM**. You'll need this number when you choose a model.

   ![Task Manager's GPU page with the card's name and Dedicated GPU memory](../../assets/docs/getting-started/windows-task-manager-gpu.png)

{% /steps %}

An NVIDIA card needs `koboldcpp.exe`. For an AMD or Intel card, or if there is no **GPU** entry, use `koboldcpp-nocuda.exe`.

On Linux, `lspci | grep -iE 'vga|3d'` shows the card's name, and `nvidia-smi` shows an NVIDIA card's memory. On a Mac with Apple Silicon, the graphics chip uses the Mac's main memory.

All files and what each contains: [Release files and system requirements](/docs/install/releases/).
